  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1)\nAreas of fog will develop through the predawn hours, especially in \nthe river valleys across our south and east. The fog will burn off \nthrough mid morning, with quieter conditions expected through the \nrest of the day. \n\nSome mid level energy moving across the Great Lakes tonight will \nhelp deepen the trough over the region through the day on Saturday as\na secondary short wave pivots through the mid Ohio Valley Saturday \ninto Saturday night. As we destabilize ahead of this, MLCapes will \npush into the 1500-2000 J/KG range through the afternoon on Saturday.\nAs a result, expect scattered shower and thunderstorm development as\nwe head into the afternoon, with this activity shifting east across \nour area through late afternoon and early evening. Increasing mid \nlevel flow will allow for marginal deep layer shear of 20-30 knots, \nso a few strong to severe storms will be possible Saturday afternoon\ninto early evening. The main threat will be isolated damaging wind \ngusts, but some cooler air moving in aloft may also support some hail\nin the stronger updrafts.",
